<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hugo von Montfort</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1357–1423</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Hugo of Montfort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hugo von Montfort was a count of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bregenz">Bregenz</a> line of the Montfort family and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> official who served as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a>. He is best known as a poet: his German songs, letters and speeches, many with melodies, survive in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a> and make him one of the last of the late medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minnesanger">Minnesingers</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hugo-von-montfort.jpg" alt="Hugo von Montfort" width="263" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ferdinandbrandlandschmand · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugo_Von_Montfort.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
